WEBVTT

00:27:59.708 --> 00:28:01.768
in order to be able to take risks?

00:28:01.792 --> 00:28:03.226
That's one body of research.

00:28:03.250 --> 00:28:04.518
AG: Or is it the reverse?

00:28:04.542 --> 00:28:09.059
EP: Or is it the fact that you take risks
that grants you a greater sense of trust?

00:28:09.083 --> 00:28:12.643
But you first have to go into the unknown
to then establish the trust.

00:28:12.667 --> 00:28:13.934
AG: I can answer that one.

00:28:13.958 --> 00:28:15.226
EP: Go ahead.
AG: Yes.

00:28:15.250 --> 00:28:17.393
EP: To the second one?
AG: No, no, it's both.

00:28:17.417 --> 00:28:18.934
EP: It's both.
AG: It's a cycle.

00:28:18.958 --> 00:28:20.351
EP: Yes, I agree. I think --

00:28:20.375 --> 00:28:21.934
AG: Here you are agreeing again.

00:28:21.958 --> 00:28:23.601
EP: Because you're going complex.

00:28:23.625 --> 00:28:25.268
(Laughter)

00:28:25.292 --> 00:28:28.976
AG: So if I say something complicating,
you're more likely to agree with that.

00:28:29.000 --> 00:28:30.476
EP: No, when you do both ends.